          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"}> Todd Trimble
            ‘s definition of weak
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} category
            is an example of a notion of weak
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            induced by all the possible compositions of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
            with itself for describing weak composition of 1-morphisms. The higher cells and their composition are then obtained iteratively.
          %p
            Trimble originally called these
            %em flabby
            = succeed "-categories," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
