          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://www-lmpa.univ-littoral.fr/CT08/slides/Cheng.pdf"} Terminal coalgebras
          %p There are several equivalent ways to describe this construction.
          %h3#as_an_inverse_limit As an inverse limit
          %p
            This approach starts from the observation that the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str \infty Cat
            of strict
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAT
            of the sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
