                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Str
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dots \to Str3Cat \to Str2Cat \to Cat \to Set
          %p
            where each functor is “truncation,” i.e. discard all top-dimensional cells. We would like to imitate this, but the problem is that if we discard the
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
